1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:04,150
The world has fallen in love

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,820
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,110
I just want to understand you

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,490
Won't you open up to me?

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:26,630
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

6
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,960
Enough to make me cry

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:35,300
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,430
and put it all in tune

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,270
I lost sight of everything but my goal

10
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,940
and had something important fade away

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:58,200
Let's start all over

12
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:03,330
The world has fallen in love

13
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:06,580
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

14
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,170
I want to know everything about you

15
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,340
Won't you tell me more?

16
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,970
One inch feels like a million miles

17
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:20,890
as the days just seem to race by

18
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,310
I won't and can't ever forget

19
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,560
this brightest page of my life.

20
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:34,560
Orienteering!

21
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,270
They said we can get started!

22
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,330
Why are you so peppy today?

23
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:44,700
I'm trying to leave all that moping behind me!

24
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:49,250
All you're accomplishing is getting yourself lumped in with Kominato.

25
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:52,630
Hyper goin' now, yo yo yo!

26
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:55,800
Super orienteering!

27
00:01:54,330 --> 00:01:56,500
I'll get you into the groove in no time!

28
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,800
Just you wait!

29
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:00,390
I'd really rather you didn't.

30
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:02,330
Let's go!

31
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,240
Yeah!

32
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:06,810
No doing this half-hearted.

33
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:10,180
I'm going to make the whole team get along.

34
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:11,730
This way!

35
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:13,780
We have to come together.

36
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:17,050
From there, we can draw the start line,

37
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:19,910
and open up a new page!

38
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:26,290
Look, we found a checkpoint!

39
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:32,840
Checkpoint

40
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:28,360
Hey, you made it.

41
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:32,840
The challenge here is to guess what we've mixed into this juice.

42
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:35,300
There are five ingredients.

43
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,630
You get one point for each correct answer.

44
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:41,310
The obvious ones are apple and banana.

45
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:45,790
What else could be in it?

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,400
Something happened to Mabuchi.

47
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,020
What's wrong, Kou?

48
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:54,110
It tastes like celery.

49
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:55,560
Wait, seriously?

50
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:59,610
I can't tell...

51
00:02:59,610 --> 00:03:01,680
It's definitely in there.

52
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:04,250
Do you hate celery or something?

53
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,320
That reaction has me believing.

54
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:13,190
No fair, Murao-san! C'mon and drink your share.

55
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:26,630
It's all safe to drink, right?

56
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:30,350
Of course! I made it myself.

57
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:37,650
Thyme.

58
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,010
What, you want more time?

59
00:03:41,010 --> 00:03:43,660
No, I mean, there's thyme in it.

60
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:44,920
Thyme?

61
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,870
Oh, the spice!

62
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:52,570
Wow! You're the first team to get celery and thyme.

63
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:54,950
You're the leaders so far.

64
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:01,010
la

65
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:01,010
Here's your point card and the first keyword.

66
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:03,120
Be sure to collect them all.

67
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:03,970
Roger!

68
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:08,590
Hey... do you think we could actually win this?

69
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:09,810
We totally could!

70
00:04:10,270 --> 00:04:12,640
Do the others look up for it?

71
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,010
It's sweltering.

72
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,610
Unexpectedly enthusiastic group

73
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,610
I'm ready.

74
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:22,570
I feel like we're finally on the same page!

75
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:25,450
Yeah! Let's get to work!

76
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:28,030
Hey, wait up!

77
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:30,460
We need to follow the map.

78
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:35,010
Yoshioka, take a good look at those smiles over there.

79
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,960
Other group

80
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,960
Where could those smiles lead but a checkpoint?

81
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,200
Go go go!

82
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,390
G-Guys, wait! Look at the map!

83
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,260
Checkpoint Stamp Sheet

