00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,220
That way!

106
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:05,280
Map...

107
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:10,400
Isn't that the last checkpoint?

108
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,700
Yeah, finally here.

109
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:17,140
I feel so useless...

110
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:28,120
Have you told Yoshioka-san about what you saw yesterday?

111
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:30,590
Should I have?

112
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:35,260
Don't worry, I haven't said a word.

113
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:40,200
But I don't think Futaba-chan would tell anyone even if she knew.

114
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:44,550
What's up? Talking about something fun?

115
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,560
It's nothing, Futaba-chan.

116
00:05:52,410 --> 00:05:53,620
Okay then!

117
00:05:54,710 --> 00:05:58,370
Hearing that makes it hard to keep pressing her.

118
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:03,060
Guess I still can't bring myself to say what I really want to.

119
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:06,570
Wait, this is no time to hesitate.

120
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:09,960
Changing that part of me is exactly what I'm working towards right now!

121
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,850
Let's move on!

122
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:15,810
Nice, we got all the keywords!

123
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:19,770
Checkpoint

124
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:19,770
Huh, so they want us to put them in order?

125
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
Class

126
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
Orienteering

127
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
bi

128
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
est

129
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
gg

130
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
ke

131
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
la

132
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:23,230
the

133
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:23,230
The biggest lake?

134
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:26,690
That must be the goal!

135
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:31,620
Look! Right there!

136
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:35,750
We have plenty of points, and we're doing great on time.

137
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:38,250
Could we really do it?

138
00:06:37,910 --> 00:06:39,580
Victory

139
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:41,000
Let's go!

140
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:47,960
So, uh, where are we?

141
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:52,180
We ran around randomly, so we have no idea where we are.

142
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:54,670
I know! We can use our smartphones!

143
00:06:54,670 --> 00:06:56,640
We had to leave them with the teachers, remember?

144
00:06:58,070 --> 00:06:59,390
Now what?

145
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:06,110
No problem! We can go by the terrain around us, the shape of the mountains, and the location of the sun.

146
00:07:06,110 --> 00:07:08,990
This is what orienteering is all about!

147
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,710
We're completely lost.

148
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,680
Now we're screwed.

149
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:34,200
What? You tryin' to say it's my fault?

150
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,010
I said nothing of the sort.

151
00:07:36,010 --> 00:07:38,680
You all agreed to follow me!

152
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:41,190
I told you, that's not what I said.

153
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:43,380
This is no time to be fighting.

154
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,700
We need to get out of the forest, and fast.

155
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:52,870
It's not all that large, so I'm sure we can make it out if we keep moving.

156
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:54,030
But...

157
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:57,660
Is it really a good idea to wander around like that?

158
00:07:57,660 --> 00:08:03,000
Shouldn't we just wait here for the teachers to come find us?

159
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,890
I hear a river.

160
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:18,950
Considering the lake we're looking for should be that direction, there's probably a way out, too.

161
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:22,030
Let's go as far as we can while it's still light out.

162
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:28,190
If we can't escape by sunset, then we'll stop and wait, like Makita suggested.

163
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,150
How's that sound?

164
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,430
Don't you worry. We're all in this together.

165
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:41,560
Check it out, it's the river!

166
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:45,210
The current's pretty slow, so we can make it across.

167
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:46,510
Let's go.

168
00:09:01,090 --> 00:09:03,050
Easy as pie!

169
00:09:07,750 --> 00:09:10,210
Don't relax until you're safely across.

170
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:12,520
That really gave me a start.

171
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,990
Yuuri, be careful!

172
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:19,200
I'm scared! I can't do it!

173
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,040
Just take it step by step.

174
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,040
Sprint as fast as you can!

175
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,040
Take your time!

176
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,080
Don't all talk at once!

177
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:27,290
What is she doing?

178
00:09:28,490 --> 00:09:29,590
Makita!

179
00:09:30,950 --> 00:09:32,450
Here, grab on.

180
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:34,420
But I'm scared...

181
00:09:34,730 --> 00:09:36,440
Just give me your hand already.

182
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:38,180
Here.

183
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,160
I'll fall I'll fall!

184
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,520
See? You did it.

185
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:50,990
You can make it across.

186
00:09:53,930 --> 00:09:55,030
Can't you?

187
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:03,910
Makita, keep at it!

188
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:07,330
Kou, you really amaze me.

189
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:10,240
You completely calmed Yuuri down.

190
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,260
You did really well.

191
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,940
Thanks, Mabuchi-kun.

192
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:17,920
Sure.

193
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:22,080
Sorry I made you all worry.

194
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,620
I'm just glad you're safe.

195
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,770
Alright, let's get moving.

196
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:28,540
Yeah!

197
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,760
We should probably speed it up.

198
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:40,760
Uh oh... I think I hurt my foot when I fell.

199
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,060
It hurts like hell to walk!

200
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,930
Did you hurt your foot?

201
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,930
No way, not at all!

202
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:04,220
You hurt your foot.

203
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:08,310
Was it at the river?

204
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,100
Futaba-chan...

205
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:14,610
I'll find the way out and bring the teachers back.

206
00:11:16,030 --> 00:11:19,200
It'll be dark soon, so there's no time to waste.

207
00:11:19,610 --> 00:11:21,820
It'd be even worse to split up here.

208
00:11:22,570 --> 00:11:25,910
The worst-case scenario is if it gets dark before you find a way out.

209
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,960
Don't worry about me! Let's just get out of here.

210
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:35,460
Kominato, hold this for me.

211
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:39,510
Get on.

212
00:11:42,130 --> 00:11:43,640
I'll carry you back.

213
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,060
No, it's embarrassing!

214
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:49,640
You don't have the luxury to be embarrassed.

215
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:53,060
Get on or you'll just be slowing the rest of us down.

216
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:00,610
Futaba-chan, I'll hold your bag.

217
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:02,450
Oh, thanks.

218
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:06,830
Then, I'll take you up on your offer...

219
00:12:08,990 --> 00:12:10,750
I-I'm kind of heavy.

220
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:12,160
Shut up and get on.

221
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,460
You were right.

222
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,800
A-Aren't I? Let me down and I'll walk!

223
00:12:20,130 --> 00:12:25,180
I don't mind. The extra weight makes you feel more real in my hands.

224
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,140
Weird response.

225
00:12:29,010 --> 00:12:35,480
But he doesn't seem to disapprove of me being here, so I have that.

226
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:38,400
Weirdo...

227
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:44,110
He's warm.

228
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:46,990
I can smell Kou.

229
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:37,960
Yuuri.

230
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,590
Are you still awake?

231
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,710
Yeah, I'm up.

232
00:13:42,710 --> 00:13:46,550
A lot went wrong today, but it sure was fun.

233
00:13:46,550 --> 00:13:49,640
Yeah! Too bad we ended up finishing last.

234
00:13:51,850 --> 00:13:52,970
So, hey...

235
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:57,230
Back in the middle of orienteering...

236
00:13:58,850 --> 00:14:00,360
What were you and Murao-san...

237
00:14:04,530 --> 00:14:05,530
Never mind.

238
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:10,120
Futaba-chan, listen.

239
00:14:11,870 --> 00:14:16,790
I've always tended to keep to myself, but it's not like I didn't get lonely.

240
00:14:18,710 --> 00:14:21,250
When you talked to me that day,

241
00:14:21,710 --> 00:14:24,590
can you imagine just how happy I was?

242
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:26,090
That's why...

243
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:34,770
I'll never leave you alone. I promise.

244
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,650
Me too! I understand just how much it hurts to be alone.

245
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:51,570
I'll always be your friend, no matter what.

246
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,910
Thanks!

247
00:15:19,230 --> 00:15:20,270
Kou?

248
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:25,980
Kou!

249
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,820
Yoshioka.

250
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,030
What are you doing out this early?

251
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:34,830
I couldn't get back to sleep, so I figured I'd watch the sunrise.

252
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,370
How's your ankle?

253
00:15:38,370 --> 00:15:41,790
I feel fine now. The painkillers are helping.

254
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,210
That's good.

255
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:47,550
There's just a tiny tinge of light on the horizon.

256
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:50,510
I can't tell whether it's night or day.

257
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:55,800
For some reason, it reminds me of you.

258
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,060
What part?

259
00:15:57,060 --> 00:16:00,640
I can't tell whether you're kind or mean.

260
00:16:01,310 --> 00:16:03,480
That makes two of us.

261
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:07,860
I can't tell if you're incompetent or courageous.

262
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:17,280
Caught between night and day,

263
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,290
just like us.

264
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:29,090
It's pretty chilly, so put that on.

265
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:32,220
Won't you get cold then?

266
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:34,680
I'm alright.

267
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,600
Thanks.

268
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,390
We still have some time before the sun rises.

269
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,850
I know!

270
00:16:51,150 --> 00:16:53,030
Man, you totally beat us here!

271
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,330
Hey...

272
00:16:59,330 --> 00:17:02,580
Did you seriously not grab a jacket when you were in your room?

273
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:06,380
Sorry! Here, I'll give it back.

274
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:07,540
Forget it.

275
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,420
You can keep it on.

276
00:17:32,070 --> 00:17:36,530
Alright, here it comes! Almost here!

277
00:17:37,950 --> 00:17:40,700
It's here!

278
00:17:42,490 --> 00:17:44,200
Daybreak.

279
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,330
The beginning of a new day.

280
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,920
The scent of damp ground.

281
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:55,130
The scent of morning dew.

282
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:57,590
The scent of a May morning.

283
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:05,140
I don't think I'll ever forget watching this sunrise with everyone.

284
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:08,350
One day, when we look back on this...

285
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:12,730
I want everyone who shared this experience

286
00:18:12,730 --> 00:18:16,030
to remember these fun and warm times.

287
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:21,280
I really like that line. It completely
embodies what adolescence is all about.

288
00:18:21,990 --> 00:18:23,700
You really feel no shame.

289
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,460
If you get embarrassed, you lose, man.

290
00:18:29,370 --> 00:18:35,010
Don't lose your passion until you're old and wrinkled!

291
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:38,340
And I doubt you ever will.

292
00:18:52,110 --> 00:18:55,400
Anyone forget anything? If not, we're leaving.

293
00:19:03,490 --> 00:19:05,240
They're crushing me!

294
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:10,540
Sakigaya Station

295
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:14,500
Yeah. Thanks a lot.

296
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:18,720
My mom's coming to pick me up.

297
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,800
I see.

298
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:27,100
It doesn't even hurt that much.

299
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:30,730
Still, you shouldn't push it.

300
00:19:30,730 --> 00:19:32,980
Yeah, you're right.

301
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:36,400
Kou, aren't you going home?

302
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,780
Hey, a cat.

303
00:19:41,610 --> 00:19:44,700
Don't tell me... you're going to keep me company?

304
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,700
Don't worry about it, you can go—

305
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:49,500
Look!

306
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:53,920
Check it out. He's only got one sock on.

307
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,760
He's still just a kitty.

308
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,310
Wonder if he's stray.

309
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:08,520
Seems to like people, though.

310
00:20:10,430 --> 00:20:13,150
I'm learning more about Kou.

311
00:20:13,150 --> 00:20:14,480
He hates celery.

312
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,690
He likes cats.

313
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:20,190
He may have a rough way of speaking,

314
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,030
but in reality...

315
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:23,990
...he's gentle.

316
00:20:30,410 --> 00:20:31,710
My ride's here.

317
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:37,090
Guess I'll head back too.

318
00:20:37,590 --> 00:20:38,550
Later.

319
00:20:41,590 --> 00:20:42,510
Kou!

320
00:20:43,050 --> 00:20:45,430
Thanks for waiting with me.

321
00:20:45,890 --> 00:20:49,390
Huh? I was just playing with that cat.

322
00:20:50,770 --> 00:20:52,560
That's what I thought you'd say!

323
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:58,820
He's no longer the Kou I remember.
Both his voice and height have changed.

324
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:02,780
But now I can say I know...

325
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:05,530
...the sixteen-year-old Kou.

326
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:09,740
The one who made my heart skip a beat...

327
00:21:11,370 --> 00:21:13,120
...was the sixteen-year-old Kou.

328
00:21:14,330 --> 00:21:17,710
Have I fallen in love with...

329
00:21:27,140 --> 00:21:28,640
A text from Yuuri.

330
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
A lot happened at the camp,

331
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
Back Home

332
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
I feel like we all got a lot closer to each other

333
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
Is your leg alright?

334
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
Yuuri

335
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:33,600
but it was a ton of fun!

336
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:37,440
"I'm not even mad at Kominato-kun anymore."

337
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:46,990
And, also...

338
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:46,990
I think I fell for Mabuchi-kun!

339
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:46,990
Well, I...

340
00:22:00,670 --> 00:22:05,800
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

341
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:11,180
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

342
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:16,640
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

343
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:21,940
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

344
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:31,660
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

345
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:37,250
but it passed, as days tend to do.

346
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:47,800
The rails carry you away

347
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:56,060
leaving me alone on our usual path.

348
00:22:57,180 --> 00:23:06,690
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

349
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:15,410
so why can't I say them?

350
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:22,380
Why can't I?

351
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:39,940
NEXT TIME...

352
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:31,840
The first time I realized my feelings
was when he helped me cross that river.

353
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:36,310
He's really kind and he makes my heart race,

354
00:23:36,310 --> 00:23:38,980
but more than that, he's reliable.
